'''East Fosian Baliscans''' ({{Langx|bl|Baliscanos Fosianos Orientales}}) are [[Baliscans]] who were either born in or can trace their [[W:Ancestor|ancestry]] to [[East Fosia]]. East Fosian Baliscans are also a subgroup of [[Asian Baliscans|Fosian Baliscans]]. According to [[Confederal Institute of Statistics|ICS]], East Fosian Baliscans and can be further divided by on the basis of both ethnicity and nationality, such as [[Jade Baliscans]], [[Sanese Baliscans]], tba Baliscan, tba Baliscan, [[Kwangjuan Baliscans|Kwangjuan Baliscan]], [[Mongolian Baliscans|"Mongolian" Baliscan]], tba, or tba Baliscan, as seen on demi-decadal [[Census in Balisca|census data]].

According to the [[2025 Baliscan census]], 10,774,942 Baliscans had traced their ancestry to East Fosia, constituting 6.97&nbsp;percent of the total population and 31.47&nbsp;percent of the total Fosian Baliscan population. 

